# #1355: EVERY container's resources go through aether.resources, not only the
# four above (and install-supervisor, below). The seven that still used plain
# `toYaml` rendered `cpu: ""` for `--set <x>.resources.limits.cpu=`, which the
# apiserver rejects as a quantity. One test per container: with the CPU limit
# emptied, `limits:` carries memory only. Each pattern is positional (it ends on
# the line that follows that container's block), so it cannot be satisfied by
# another container of the same pod.

